factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The headline and reel_script attribute the suicide to 'படிப்பு, மொபைல் பிரச்சனை' (study and mobile problems) and the caption repeats it; the article only says the parents scolded him for using his mobile phone and he was not interested in studies, and gives no cause of death beyond that, so the cause is overstated.
  The reel_script and caption say the student was 'மீட்டு' (rescued) and taken to hospital, but the article says he was already dead when found; the caption wording 'மீட்கப்பட்டார்' is acceptable, but the reel_script's 'அக்கம் பக்கத்தினரின் உதவியுடன் மீட்டு' is fine; however the caption's claim that the news 'இச்சம்பவம் தெரியவந்தது' at 6 pm is an added detail not in the article.
  The caption states the student was taken to Namakkal hospital, and the reel_script says he was found dead by parents at 6 pm; the article says the parents returned at 6 pm and found him, which matches, but the reel_script's phrase 'வெளியே சென்றார்' is ambiguous and the slide 'அடுத்து என்ன?' header is not a factual claim, so no issue there.
  The slides_spec 'hl2' line 'பெற்றோர் கண்டித்ததால்' implies the scolding caused the suicide, a causal claim the article does not establish.
  The caption's 'நேற்று முன்தினம் காலை வெளியே சென்ற அவர், வீட்டில் சேலையில் தூக்கிட்ட நிலையில் சடலமாக மீட்கப்பட்டார்' merges two separate events (leaving in the morning and being found hanging) into one sentence without the article saying when he was found, which the article only indicates was at parents' return around 6 pm.
